WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.372
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>This is a LEGO film about making a LEGO film.

2
00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:08.543
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Homer's Odyssey, built from LEGO bricks, and taught, one scene at a time, to act.

3
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.433
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>It began with a problem.

4
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.457
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The first scene had almost everything a film needs:

5
00:00:16.457 --> 00:00:23.216
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>a set built from real LEGO parts, recorded voices, faces that move their lips, captions and music.

6
00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:26.664
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Athena waits at the gate, disguised as a stranger.

7
00:00:26.664 --> 00:00:29.216
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>And the characters do nothing at all.

8
00:00:29.216 --> 00:00:30.113
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Nobody turns.

9
00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:31.009
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Nobody moves.

10
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.191
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Here is the same moment, three days later.

11
00:00:35.191 --> 00:00:41.085
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Telemachus sees the stranger, rises, crosses the hall, welcomes her, and takes her spear.

12
00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:44.131
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Every one of those movements now has a reason.

13
00:00:44.131 --> 00:00:45.786
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>This is how it got there.

14
00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.875
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Every scene starts as a card.

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.116
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>A card says who is there, where they stand, and what is said.

16
00:00:54.116 --> 00:01:04.616
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The cast are minifigures assembled from real parts, and the set is foraged from community LEGO models, checked stud by stud, so that every piece could really be built.

17
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:09.897
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Then a handful of keyframe stills fix the beats of the story:

18
00:01:09.897 --> 00:01:14.918
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Athena arrives, the suitors feast, Telemachus notices her, and he welcomes her.

19
00:01:14.918 --> 00:01:18.223
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Each still is checked against the words of the poem.

20
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.320
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The first acting was keyed by hand, on a dope sheet, channel by channel, against the voice.

21
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.452
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The figures moved, but they moved without reasons.

22
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.739
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>So the score was rewritten in lanes, read from the top down.

23
00:01:33.739 --> 00:01:34.776
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>First the voice:

24
00:01:34.776 --> 00:01:35.618
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>what is said.

25
00:01:35.618 --> 00:01:36.655
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Then the intent:

26
00:01:36.655 --> 00:01:38.340
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>what each character wants.

27
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.247
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Then the body:

28
00:01:39.247 --> 00:01:42.488
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>the head, the arms, the weight, that carry it out.

29
00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:45.210
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Every movement must point back to a cause.

30
00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:52.955
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The performance engine compiles those intents into the bodies on the rigs, and measures what it made.

31
00:01:52.955 --> 00:01:55.154
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Movement with no cause is a defect.

32
00:01:55.154 --> 00:01:56.850
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>A stillness needs a reason.

33
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.682
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Then a camera has to find the performance.

34
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.333
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The cinematographer chooses its shots from the score.

35
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:11.717
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>It goes where the action is hottest, cuts when the action moves, and tests every camera against the set.

36
00:02:11.717 --> 00:02:17.977
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Marks on the bodies show what a camera can see, and every finished film is checked on a contact sheet:

37
00:02:17.977 --> 00:02:19.573
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>one frame from every shot.

38
00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.750
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Still, a camera can be wrong.

39
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:29.010
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>On the raft, Calypso stood pressed against Odysseus, and her lines played behind his head and his bow.

40
00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.429
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>In the new take they stand a step apart, and she speaks on her own face.

41
00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:42.334
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The Horse Song held one wide of a wooden horse for fifty seconds, because the man the song is about had not been drawn yet.

42
00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:47.459
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The new take moves into the king's hall, where Odysseus weeps, and the king notices.

43
00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.808
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>In the land of the dead, Achilles never said the line the scene is famous for.

44
00:02:53.808 --> 00:02:56.535
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Now he answers, on a close of his own face:

45
00:02:56.535 --> 00:03:00.786
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>he would rather be a hired man, alive, than king over all the dead.

46
00:03:00.786 --> 00:03:03.196
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>And the dead are drawn as pale shades.

47
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.523
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Some fixes needed the engine to learn something new.

48
00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.309
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>A thrown thing can fly.

49
00:03:10.309 --> 00:03:16.045
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Antinous seizes the footstool, and it is seen in the air, on its arc, to the beggar's shoulder.

50
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.031
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>A set piece can be carried.

51
00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:23.189
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The giant's great stone moves with his arms into the mouth of the cave.

52
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.029
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>And the dead are shades.

53
00:03:26.029 --> 00:03:31.246
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Three times Odysseus reaches for his mother, and three times his arms pass through her.

54
00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.915
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>None of the old takes are thrown away.

55
00:03:34.915 --> 00:03:40.159
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Each one is kept beside the take that replaced it, with a note on what changed, and why.

56
00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:49.696
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>Thirty-three takes of sixteen scenes, and forty-four performed films, from the council of the gods to the bed that cannot be moved.

57
00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:52.056
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The Odyssey, in LEGO, learning to act.

58
00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.125
<v Narrator (synthetic voice)>The narration you have been hearing is a synthetic voice.

